        77.4,
        297.6
      ],
      "text": "Subject:- Revised Proforma for furnishing details of officers by the Cadre Controlling\nAuthorities while seeking vigilance clearance-modification of Point No. 13- reg."
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 18,
      "poly": [
        282.6,
        300.3,
        304.7,
        300.3,
        304.7,
        305.2,
        282.6,
        305.2
      ],
      "text": "****"
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 19,
      "poly": [
        79.3,
        325.6,
        516.0,
        324.9,
        516.0,
        416.6,
        79.3,
        417.2
      ],
      "text": "Kind attention is invited to the Central Vigilance Commission's OM of even number\ndated 30.09.2021 vide which 13-point proforma for capturing departmental inputs on\nantecedence of concerned officer has been circulated. The revised proforma has two distinct\nparts (Part-I & II) which are to be submitted separately, under the signature of CVO/HOD.\nPrior to this, the departmental inputs were captured in 12-point proforma. The additional\npoint (Point No 13) of the revised proforma captures information on complaint(s) pending\nagainst the concerned officer, along with its relevant details (i.e. age/status/gist etc)."
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 20,
      "poly": [
        79.3,
        426.4,
        516.4,
        426.1,
        516.4,
        478.3,
        79.3,
        478.7
      ],
      "text": "2.\nThe Central Vigilance Commission discharges its functions and duties, as mandated\nunder the CVC Act, 2003, amended from time to time. Para 3.3 (a) of the comprehensive\nguidelines issued by the Central Vigilance Commission vide its circular No. 25/12/21 dated\n24.12.2021 (F. No. 021/VGL/051) on complaint handling mechanism reads as under:"
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 21,
      "poly": [
        112.1,
        488.5,
        518.7,
        487.9,
        518.7,
        512.8,
        112.1,
        513.5
      ],
      "text": "\"Central Vigilance Commission deals with complaints in the matters of corruption\nand irregular acts having vigilance angle.\""
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 22,
      "poly": [
        79.7,
        523.3,
        516.8,
        522.7,
        516.8,
        574.6,
        79.7,
        575.2
      ],
      "text": "Similarly, Para 1.4.9 of Chapter-I of Vigilance Manual (updated 2021) also stipulates that\nadministrative misconduct would be dealt by the disciplinary authority in an appropriate\nmanner. If lapse is without vigilance angle, the disciplinary authority would be within its\nrights to initiate appropriate penalty proceedings against erring employees."
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 23,
      "poly": [
        79.3,
        583.1,
        519.1,
        582.8,
        519.1,
        608.7,
        79.3,
        609.1
      ],
      "text": "3.\nKeeping in view the above, the Commission has decided to modify Point 13 of\nproforma, as under:"
    }
